{"name":"Follow the Leader","hex":"#f7e5d0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"follow the leader","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Alternative spelling of follow-the-leader."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/follow_the_leader"}],"entries":[{"title":"Follow the Leader (1930 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Follow the Leader is a 1930 American pre-Code musical comedy film co-directed by Norman Taurog and Albert Parker. It stars Ginger Rogers and Ed Wynn in his film debut. The screenplay by Gertrude Purcell and Sid Silvers is based on a play by William K. Wells, George White and Lew Brown, with songs by Buddy DeSylva and Ray Henderson. It was produced and distributed by Paramount Publix Corporation."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Follow_the_Leader_(1930_film)"},{"title":"Follow the Leader (1944 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Follow the Leader is a 1944 American film directed by William Beaudine featuring the East Side Kids."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/ac/Follow_the_Leader_FilmPoster.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Follow_the_Leader_(1944_film)"},{"title":"Follow the Leader (Korn album)","blocks":[{"text":"Follow the Leader is the third studio album by American nu metal band Korn. It was released on August 18, 1998, through both Immortal and Epic Records. This was their first album not produced by Ross Robinson, instead being produced by Steve Thompson and Toby Wright."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/52/Korn_follow_the_leader.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Follow_the_Leader_(Korn_album)"},{"title":"Leadership","blocks":[{"text":"Leadership is the ability of an individual, group, or organization to influence, or guide other individuals, teams, or organizations. Leadership is a contested term. Specialist literature debates various viewpoints on the concept, sometimes contrasting Eastern and Western approaches to leadership, and also North American versus European approaches."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Wishnu_Wardhana_-_Opening_APEC_CEO_Summit_2013.jpg/330px-Wishnu_Wardhana_-_Opening_APEC_CEO_Summit_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leadership"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Cheech_Marin_2012.jpg/500px-Cheech_Marin_2012.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Cheech_Marin_2012.jpg/1280px-Cheech_Marin_2012.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Cheech_Marin_2012.jpg/500px-Cheech_Marin_2012.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The hidden track \"Earache My Eye\" features comedian Cheech Marin of Cheech & Chong.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACheech_Marin_2012.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/IceCube_Toronto2006.jpg/500px-IceCube_Toronto2006.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/IceCube_Toronto2006.jpg/1280px-IceCube_Toronto2006.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/IceCube_Toronto2006.jpg/500px-IceCube_Toronto2006.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rapper Ice Cube is featured on the track \"Children of the Korn\".","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIceCube_Toronto2006.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Managem